<Industry key="dental" title="AI receptionists for dental practices" faqs={faqs} guide={["<strong>Books into your schedule:</strong> does it book straight into your dental software (Dentrix, Eaglesoft, Open Dental, Curve, Denticon) or just take a message?","<strong>Privacy agreement in writing:</strong> a service that hears patient details must sign a HIPAA privacy agreement with you (a BAA). A 'HIPAA compliant' badge is not the same as a signed agreement.","<strong>Emergency handoff:</strong> test that urgent calls reach a person, after hours.","<strong>Recording:</strong> if the tool records or transcribes, check the caller's state on the <a href='/call-recording-consent-by-state/'>call recording consent</a> page.","Standalone dental AI receptionists typically run about $200–$800/month per location, per <a href='https://www.keragon.com/blog/ai-receptionist-dental'>Keragon</a>."]}/>
